From d1d5b64cf46e6092fde7286f258b39c9d21d0f9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yzddmr6 <46088090+yzddmr6@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 09:31:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] turnip/ir3: use exact-width typed reads for aligned readonly
 SSBOs

Add R32, RG32 and RGBA32 aliases to storage-buffer descriptors and select
ordinary typed reads for aligned readonly vectors. Decompose vectors
without reading extra components; retain the existing path for unaligned
accesses and robustness2.

Expand the descriptor stride from two to five slots and use multiplication
for resource index and reindex addressing. Update dynamic offsets, mutable
pool sizing, descriptor-buffer sizes and null descriptors consistently.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
